  "id": "post-event-planetscope-2026-08-28",
  "title": "Corridor and lower Trishuli, two days after — Post-event Imagery",
  "description": "PlanetScope coverage acquired 04:57–05:01 UTC on 28 August 2026, two days after the flood. A four-frame strip (satellite 2544) runs south down the Bhote Koshi–Trishuli corridor from above Rasuwagadhi to Betrawati, with a fifth frame (satellite 2520) offset to the south-west, extending coverage along the lower Trishuli past Trishuli Bazaar to 27.711 N — the southernmost extent in this catalog. Cloud is 64–90% with clear fractions of 4–25%: heavy, but better than the same-day 26 August coverage, and the corridor and its river channel are legible through breaks in the upper strip. Unlike the 26 August scenes, all five are quality_category standard. Analytic products are top-of-atmosphere radiance; surface reflectance was not published for these scenes. 5 scenes; each Item carries the available visual, analytic, udm2 assets.",
